{"event_type":"review","id":"1ca1d7b5f74a21b11ea64fe0f8f388df6f45f3c0f125b024a428abe4f6fa602f","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T03:05:50Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/57e383eaaa6d2308f3e70bc866d64883e57dfbb991a20db57e38b213c530a745","sha256":"57e383eaaa6d2308f3e70bc866d64883e57dfbb991a20db57e38b213c530a745"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/577853ec213b49f16e0ecc669ffa6f09f7a1f770ea0862309212a14a807145de","sha256":"577853ec213b49f16e0ecc669ffa6f09f7a1f770ea0862309212a14a807145de"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6027b0d1ac5d7f7093b9c3524b5f3d282d71e4fb7719d63c3d46b018b06f92e5","sha256":"6027b0d1ac5d7f7093b9c3524b5f3d282d71e4fb7719d63c3d46b018b06f92e5"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/e3c89d5d56f131bf9f8ea6978fe395e20a15e8e22b068b5c11764d0f57281d93","sha256":"e3c89d5d56f131bf9f8ea6978fe395e20a15e8e22b068b5c11764d0f57281d93"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/45465485dab9af1b5dba02a694976b34fc17ac7493e8f832f9c3e6e5564825b3","sha256":"45465485dab9af1b5dba02a694976b34fc17ac7493e8f832f9c3e6e5564825b3"}],"attempt_id":"2da5525f804b0806845baecfd7beaa06d014600c64b9b611a983c2001f45a185:0:1","base":"f06e942e8f939aa27315b6abd7eb9bf732e26639","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"87ca62064ae06ecd723ff5b4c88f3d691ec81dfa","body":"**`QUOTED_SPAN` pairs English apostrophes as quotes. This can drop a real trigger from the survival check.**\n\n`'([^'\\n]{3,200})'` has no boundary on the opening or closing quote. A contraction such as `don't` or `finding's` therefore starts a single-quoted span. Take this finding text: `Replace \"OLD_FLAG\"; don't keep 'LEGACY' anywhere`.\n\n- `matchAll` consumes `'t keep '` as the span `t keep `.\n- Scanning resumes at `LEGACY' anywhere`, so `LEGACY` is never extracted.\n- If `LEGACY` still appears in `after` and `\"OLD_FLAG\"` sits on a removed line, `trigger-removed` passes. The verdict can then reach `resolved` even though a quoted trigger survives.\n\nContractions also count toward `MAX_SPANS`. Ordinary prose can therefore push a finding over the scan cap.\n\nThe runtime path cannot return `resolved` yet, because the assembler sets `relevantDependenciesComplete: false` (docs/address-closure-verification.md:16-19). Fix the regex before a dependency-evidence producer enables closure. Require a non-word character, or the start of the text, before an opening quote. Require a non-word character, or the end of the text, after a closing quote.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-const QUOTED_SPAN = /\"([^\"\\n]{3,200})\"|'([^'\\n]{3,200})'|`([^`\\n]{3,200})`/g;\n+const QUOTED_SPAN =\n+  /(?<![\\w])(?:\"([^\"\\n]{3,200})\"|'([^'\\n]{3,200})'|`([^`\\n]{3,200})`)(?![\\w])/g;\n```\n</details>\n\nAdd a test that combines a contraction with a surviving single-quoted trigger.","id":"63c6c942dca5598371105dcb20b5e8ad64542dd725c998dd3cf5f0993ff033f5","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`QUOTEDSPAN` pairs English apostrophes as quotes. This can drop a real trigger from the survival check."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"87ca62064ae06ecd723ff5b4c88f3d691ec81dfa","body":"**Require a boundary before declaration keywords.**\n\nIn `src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts:99`, `DECLARATION_SURVIVAL('foo')` matches `const foo` inside `myconst foo`. Unrelated text in `after` or a cited dependency can therefore produce an `unresolved` verdict.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    `(?:function\\\\*?|class|interface|type|enum|const|let|var)\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(symbol)}(?![A-Za-z0-9_$])`,\n+    `(?<![A-Za-z0-9_$])(?:function\\\\*?|class|interface|type|enum|const|let|var)\\\\s+${escapeRegExp(symbol)}(?![A-Za-z0-9_$])`,\n```\n\n</details>","id":"7fed872135f11f07269eecb52687accddfc4e81341e6c388a261b32d53456cf5","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Require a boundary before declaration keywords."}],"head":"7e40a8b4359b2fe2c7272f44f361ac2d8cb9740d","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"07911f056e3c95f7889ac56c545b819ab96507f8","intervals":[[1,185]],"path":"docs/address-closure-verification.md"},{"blob":"87ca62064ae06ecd723ff5b4c88f3d691ec81dfa","intervals":[[1,585]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts"},{"blob":"5c095b379a70aba297662be739a48a0368440810","intervals":[[1,1007]],"path":"test/ops/review/addressVerification.test.ts"}],"job_id":"2da5525f804b0806845baecfd7beaa06d014600c64b9b611a983c2001f45a185:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"9611f57bb0175f83b2d138a0aac223266c9b70e2","method":"pre-merge","pre":"6a55f72351c183cf99065244c7fa8809f2801d8a","source_path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts"},"blob":"87ca62064ae06ecd723ff5b4c88f3d691ec81dfa","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressVerification.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"9611f57bb0175f83b2d138a0aac223266c9b70e2","method":"pre-merge","pre":"6a55f72351c183cf99065244c7fa8809f2801d8a","source_path":"docs/address-closure-verification.md"},"blob":"07911f056e3c95f7889ac56c545b819ab96507f8","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"docs/address-closure-verification.md","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"9611f57bb0175f83b2d138a0aac223266c9b70e2","method":"pre-merge","pre":"6a55f72351c183cf99065244c7fa8809f2801d8a","source_path":"test/ops/review/addressVerification.test.ts"},"blob":"5c095b379a70aba297662be739a48a0368440810","disposition"